Notebook[{
Cell["ArrayDomain", "ObjectName",ExpressionUUID->"800a7c26-19fb-1c47-81bf-2315f914e00f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox[
   RowBox[{"ArrayDomain", "[", "arr", "]"}], "InlineCode"]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"893be31c-01be-b04b-bf87-21b81fd02ea4"],
 " ",
 "gives the narrowest recognized value domain containing every entry of arr, \
or \"Expression\" if the entries lie in none of them."
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"0a9b30c6-f8ff-2f4b-aa26-c85f79d91519"],

Cell["Details and Options", "NotesSection",ExpressionUUID->"94de600d-8bee-d14e-9971-1a1df6739f51"],

Cell["\<\
The recognized domains are \"Boolean\", \"Integer\", \"Rational\", \"Real\" \
and \"Complex\", together with FiniteField[p, n].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"082bae80-fe76-434a-b850-ce7dcc15ded3"],

Cell["\<\
\"Boolean\" means the entries are True and False. Entries 0 and 1 are \
integers, and the elements of the two-element field are FiniteField[2, 1].\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8bc2ab3a-7ae2-764d-a2df-8ae11ba48d6a"],

Cell["\<\
It is computed from the entries, not declared: an array is not told what it \
is made of. An array whose entries answer to none of the recognized domains \
is an array of expressions, which is a perfectly good array; generated \
symbolic entries and labels are both of that kind.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"1e30be3a-37a2-5b46-a39f-262c5780900e"],

Cell["\<\
Because it is computed rather than stored, it costs a pass over the entries \
to ask.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"f0e1f09b-3684-f041-93bf-8f67f1a4f31d"],

Cell["Examples", "PrimaryExamplesSection",ExpressionUUID->"64141203-0169-e04d-a031-fba62185d6bb"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[#] & /@ {{True, False}, {1, 2}, {1/2, 3}, {1.5, 2}, \
{1 + I, 2}}\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"0a6bc332-1e60-2441-9b44-13281127b403"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"\<\"Boolean\"\>", ",", "\<\"Integer\"\>", ",", "\<\"Rational\"\>", 
   ",", "\<\"Real\"\>", ",", "\<\"Complex\"\>"}], "}"}]], "Output",ExpressionU\
UID->"7c69706b-7060-3341-bf3d-6a7513ad0fd7"],

Cell["Entries of a finite field:", "ExampleText",ExpressionUUID->"b344de39-24b5-354d-87ee-8f1064b5c4e9"],

Cell["\<\
ArrayDomain @ ArrayObject[{FiniteField[2, 1][0], FiniteField[2, 1][1]}]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"1b92218d-7e28-0b49-9155-91fc78644f81"],

